const EXPLAIN = `<nav class="ex-toc" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#ex-read">How to read this page</a><a href="#ex-scale">The forecasts</a><a href="#ex-words">Words used here</a><a href="#ex-parts">The parts of the page</a><button type="button" class="linkish" data-faq="count">Managed Democracy for Dummies</button></nav>
<section class="ex-start" id="ex-read"><h3>How to read this page</h3>
<ol><li><b>The call</b> at the top is the one move that changes the Major Order most right now, with the order's forecast beside it.</li>
<li><b>The tabs</b> right under it hold the detail. <b>Races</b> (the first) shows every objective: each bar ends at its goal, and the lighter band is today's pace by the deadline, and the coloured edge on the left is the front. Then the full plan, progress charts, the command log and the war map.</li></ol></section>
<section id="ex-scale"><h3>The forecasts</h3>
<dl class="ex-scale">
<div class="vl-done"><dt><span class="pill vl-done"><span>Done</span></span></dt><dd>The objective, or the whole order, is complete.</dd></div>
<div class="vl-ok"><dt><span class="pill vl-ok"><span>On track</span></span></dt><dd>At today's pace we make it in time.</dd></div>
<div class="vl-push"><dt><span class="pill vl-push"><span>Needs a push</span></span></dt><dd>Winnable, with more Helldivers than today, or with everyone on the call. Also when today's pace makes it just in time, with no margin: one bad night and we miss it.</dd></div>
<div class="vl-record"><dt><span class="pill vl-record"><span>Needs a record</span></span></dt><dd>Only a record turnout wins it: about as much of the playerbase as the best order ever drew.</dd></div>
<div class="vl-out"><dt><span class="pill vl-out"><span>Out of reach</span></span></dt><dd>It would take more than any order has ever drawn, or more than every Helldiver online. The page says so, and points to the move still worth making.</dd></div>
</dl>
<p>Before a few hours of pace are measured, an objective is <b>Too early to call</b>, and it is never called out of reach in its first 3 hours. When an order ends, every objective is <b>Done</b> or <b>Failed</b>.</p></section>
<section id="ex-words"><h3>Words used here</h3>
<dl>
<dt>Regen</dt><dd>On liberation campaigns, positive enemy regen restores health every hour. If Helldiver damage is lower, liberation can slide backwards until it reaches zero. Some planets have zero or negative regen; defenses use a separate health pool and deadline.</dd>
<dt>DSS</dt><dd>The Democracy Space Station, voted from planet to planet. Measured on the war log since 2025, it adds nothing visible to liberation on its own.</dd>
<dt>Heavy Ordnance</dt><dd>The DSS's bombardment: its planet counts about 1.8 times while every other planet drops to about 0.7 (the war's total damage barely moves).</dd>
<dt>Joel</dt><dd>Arrowhead's Game Master, who steers the war by hand through Super Earth Command: goals cut or raised, planets that jump, new attacks. The Command log lists his moves.</dd>
<dt>Front</dt><dd>All the planets of one enemy faction. Kill counts usually count anywhere on that front.</dd>
<dt>Impact multiplier</dt><dd>How much each mission is worth: the game lowers it when more people play. The page reads it live, so the numbers follow today's playerbase.</dd>
</dl></section>
<section id="ex-parts"><h3>The parts of the page</h3>
<dl>
<dt>Best bet</dt><dd>When several orders run at once, the desk compares them, counting Helldivers who help two orders at once (killing bots on a bot planet counts for both). If there aren't enough Helldivers for all of them, the best bet is marked on its tab and the page opens on it.</dd>
<dt>Forecast</dt><dd>Beside the call: the order's call on the five-step scale, and the bars that explain it, Helldivers there against Helldivers needed, or today's pace against the pace needed.</dd>
<dt>When a planet falls</dt><dd>Three things go into it: the planet's own pace over the last 6 hours (it already carries the DSS, Joel's multipliers and how hard the planet is), everyone's strength that week, and the Helldivers still to come. The range is an estimate, not a guaranteed completion window. Historical coverage comes from a retrospective sample of completed liberations; see the Archive for sample sizes and live checks.</dd>
<dt>Plan</dt><dd>Every useful move ranked by importance, with what it changes. "What if…?" shows what happens with more or fewer Helldivers.</dd>
<dt>Progress</dt><dd>How the order got here: progress since it began, the pace it needs, where today's pace leads, hour by hour. Hover or tap a chart to read any moment.</dd>
<dt>Command log</dt><dd>Hand-made changes by Super Earth Command or a scripted enemy push, and the latest Super Earth news. The war is recorded every 10 minutes even while nobody has the page open.</dd>
<dt>Map</dt><dd>Every planet being fought over, at its place in the galaxy, in its owner's colour and sized by its Helldivers. A ring marks the order's planets, brackets the planet of the call, dashed lines the attacks.</dd>
<dt>Kills, samples, operations</dt><dd>The pace needed is compared with the last 24 hours (a full day and night), or the average since the start until a day has been recorded, and the last hour.</dd>
<dt>Option orders</dt><dd>Some orders say Option 1, Option 2: any one of them wins. The forecast and the plan follow the most winnable option.</dd>
<dt>Regions</dt><dd>Planets with regions are taken one region at a time, quickest first; splitting Helldivers across regions slows everything down.</dd>
<dt>Share image, Copy for Discord</dt><dd>The call as a picture or as text, ready for Reddit, Discord or chat, with the desk's best bet when several orders run.</dd>
<dt>Links</dt><dd>The address follows the order and the tab you are on (for example <code>#order=…&amp;tab=plan</code>), so you can link to a call directly.</dd>
<dt>Shortcuts</dt><dd><kbd>Q</kbd> and <kbd>E</kbd> switch tab, <kbd>1</kbd> to <kbd>5</kbd> open a tab, <kbd>P</kbd> opens the planet's conditions and loadout, <kbd>A</kbd> the archive, <kbd>R</kbd> refreshes, <kbd>?</kbd> opens this guide.</dd>
</dl></section>
<p class="ex-limits">Limits: the effect of the DSS and Heavy Ordnance isn't public, the region capture bonus is estimated, weapon-only kill counts can't be turned into a number of Helldivers, and the Game Master can change regen at any time.</p>`;
